# Indecomposable representation
%%%
tag := "Chapter2/Definition2.3.8"
number := false
%%%
*Definition 2.3.8.* A nonzero representation $`V` of an algebra $`A` is said to be *indecomposable* if it is not isomorphic to a direct sum of two nonzero representations.

